# Day 31 – FIRST_VALUE() and LAST_VALUE()

## What I Learned
Today I learned about:

- What FIRST_VALUE() is
- What LAST_VALUE() is
- How they work with OVER()
- How they work with PARTITION BY
- Why ORDER BY is important
- Understanding window frame (ROWS BETWEEN)

FIRST_VALUE and LAST_VALUE are window functions used to retrieve
the first or last value within a window.

---

## Basic Structure

```sql
FIRST_VALUE(column_name)
OVER (
    PARTITION BY column_name
    ORDER BY column_name
)

LAST_VALUE(column_name)
OVER (
    PARTITION BY column_name
    ORDER BY column_name
)
